--- diagnostics ---
SC0420 @56..62 `String` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a C string is NUL-terminated and a Science `String` is UTF-8 bytes with a length; write `ffi.CStr` for one that is borrowed and `ffi.CString` for one Science owns, and expect the copy both of them make
SC0420 @81..101 `Map` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a `Map` is a Science hash table, and the C side does not know its layout
SC0420 @120..133 `Option` cannot cross the C boundary
  note an `Option` is a niche, and which niche depends on the payload; the C spelling of absence is a null `ffi.Pointer`
SC0420 @138..158 `Result` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a `Result` is a Science choice; a C function reports failure with a status the safe wrapper converts
SC0420 @175..185 a tuple cannot cross the C boundary
  note C has no tuple; declare a `type` marked `implements ffi.CLayout` and pass a pointer to it
SC0420 @204..217 `any Summarize` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a dynamically dispatched value is a Science pair of pointers, and C knows neither half
SC0421 @235..247 `Array of T` has no C representation
  note the length does not cross the ABI — it exists on the Science side so that the wrapper's bounds check is an expression the compiler checks
  note a call site still passes the array: `borrowed Array of T` coerces to `ffi.Span of T` there, and `.span()` names the conversion where it has to be written out
SC0420 @266..272 `String` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a C string is NUL-terminated and a Science `String` is UTF-8 bytes with a length; write `ffi.CStr` for one that is borrowed and `ffi.CString` for one Science owns, and expect the copy both of them make
SC0420 @297..307 `Box` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a `Box` owns what it points at under Science's allocator; pass `ffi.Pointer of T` and say in the binding who frees it
